      "notes": "Instagram's reel-container step fetches the video itself from a URL, same as the image path -- AURON never uploads bytes. Note: Drive's uc?export=view link can serve an HTML can't-scan-for-viruses interstitial instead of raw bytes for very large files; not handled here."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Build the direct-fetchable video URL from the Drive file id, same\n// trick as 'Build Public Image URL1'.\nconst body = $('Webhook: /instagram-post1').first().json.body;\nconst item = body.media_items[0];\nconst fileId = item.post_ref;\n\nconst out = {\n  video_url: `https://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&id=${fileId}`,\n  caption: body.caption,\n  request_id: body.request_id,\n};\n\n// thumb_offset selects the Reel cover frame, in milliseconds. Set ONLY when\n// AURON actually picked a cover: the Graph API defaults thumb_offset to 0,\n// which is the opening frame -- regularly black or blurred on phone footage,\n// and the exact thing the cover analysis exists to avoid. Sending a 0 or a\n// null would therefore be worse than sending nothing at all, so the key is\n// omitted entirely and the container node builds its query as JSON to make\n// that omission possible.\nconst cover = item.cover_timestamp_seconds;\nif (typeof cover === 'number' && cover > 0) {\n  out.thumb_offset = Math.round(cover * 1000);\n}\n\nreturn { json: out };"
      },
      "id": "b1e6a001-1111-4a11-8a11-111111111103",
      "name": "Build Public Video URL",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        944,
        -800
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
